-- title:
--   Transvections generate SL₂(ℤ/Nℤ)
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a natural number with $N \neq 0$. Inside the special linear group $\mathrm{SL}(2, \mathbb{Z}/N\mathbb{Z})$ consider the set [`ModularCurve.elemSet (ZMod N)`](def/ModularCurve_SL2Elementary.html#L63), which by definition is the union of the image of the map `upperElem`, sending $c \in \mathbb{Z}/N\mathbb{Z}$ to the matrix $\begin{pmatrix} 1 & c \\ 0 & 1\end{pmatrix}$ (of determinant $1$), and the image of the map `lowerElem`, sending $c$ to $\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 0 \\ c & 1\end{pmatrix}$. The assertion is that the subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}(2, \mathbb{Z}/N\mathbb{Z})$ generated by this set is the whole group, i.e. every matrix of determinant $1$ over $\mathbb{Z}/N\mathbb{Z}$ is a finite product of upper and lower elementary matrices (transvections) with entries in $\mathbb{Z}/N\mathbb{Z}$. Note that the generating set is taken over all $c$ in $\mathbb{Z}/N\mathbb{Z}$, and that no primality or squarefreeness hypothesis on $N$ is imposed, only $N \neq 0$ so that $\mathbb{Z}/N\mathbb{Z}$ is a nontrivial finite ring.
--
--   This is the classical statement that $\mathrm{SL}_2$ over $\mathbb{Z}/N\mathbb{Z}$ is generated by elementary matrices. It serves as the generation input for results on images of Galois representations, and is used by [`ModularCurve.SerreImage.contains_SL2`](thm.html#ModularCurve.SerreImage.contains_SL2) and by [`WeierstrassCurve.exists_algEquiv_map_eq_zsmul_add_zsmul_of_transcendental_j`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.exists_algEquiv_map_eq_zsmul_add_zsmul_of_transcendental_j).
